{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentMonodromyEquivariance"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_zeta4_bar_equivariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_zeta4_bar_equivariance","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate.lean#L150-L159","doc":"**The first vertical edge, named**: `rho_compat` is exactly\nℤ/2-equivariance of the assignment for the bar involution at the ζ₄\nfibre — already proved as a law of every `TauAssignmentData`; this\nrestatement gives it its Habiro-facing name. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.zeta4_inv_eq_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.zeta4_inv_eq_star","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate.lean#L145-L148","doc":"At `ζ₄ = i` the Habiro bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` is complex\nconjugation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.pairCoherent_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.pairCoherent_comp","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate.lean#L137-L141","doc":"Pair-coherence is closed under post-composition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.pairCoherent_of_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.pairCoherent_of_cell","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate.lean#L122-L135","doc":"**Master sufficient condition**: every functional factoring through\nthe cell restriction is pair-coherent. Subsumes the assignment and\ntrace instances; the gate a Δ_λ candidate routed through marked-pair\ncell data must pass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.monodromyN_equivariant_iff_descent_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.monodromyN_equivariant_iff_descent_transport","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate.lean#L80-L118","doc":"**The decision**: monodromy equivariance along a marking\nhomomorphism holds for all states iff the homomorphism transports the\ndescent condition pointwise. Reduces the conjugation-edge question to\nfinite combinatorics per edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.monodromyN_equivariant_of_length_preserving","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.monodromyN_equivariant_of_length_preserving","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentGaugeGate.lean#L67-L78","doc":"Any LENGTH-PRESERVING marking homomorphism is monodromy-\nequivariant. Subsumes the diagram-edge theorem and covers\nlongest-element conjugation in finite systems. ","signatureChunk":0}]}